 "stimulus_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"5\">\n  <li>A tennis ball is hit straight up in the air, and its height, in feet above the ground, is modeled by the equation <span data-math=\"f(t)=4+12t−16t^2\">f(t)=4+12t−16t^2</span>, where <span data-math=\"t\">t</span> is measured in seconds since the ball was thrown.</li>\n</ol>\n<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" type=\"a\">\n  <li><strong>Select two</strong> solutions to the equation <span data-math=\"0=4+12t−16t^2\">0=4+12t−16t^2</span>.</li>\n</ol>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 646785,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol type=\"a\">\n  <li><span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{4}\">\\frac{1}{4}</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"4\">4</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"16\">16</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"1\">1</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"-\\frac{1}{4}\">-\\frac{1}{4}</span></li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 646786,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"2\" type=\"a\">\n  <li>What do the solutions tell us about the tennis ball? <strong>Select two</strong> that apply.</li>\n</ol>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n  <li>The ball hits the ground <span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{4}\">\\frac{1}{4}</span> second after it is hit.</li>\n  <li>The negative solution does not have meaning because a negative value for time does not make sense.</li>\n  <li>The ball hits the ground 1 second after it is hit.</li>\n  <li>The negative solution is a result of the bounce of the ball.</li>\n  <li>The ball hits the ground <span data-math=\"-\\frac{1}{4}\">-\\frac{1}{4}</span> second after it is hit.</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
